Saros

This software is derived from an extended version of CCBench
(https://github.com/thawk105/ccbench), a benchmark platform for concurrency
control protocols by Takayuki Tanabe and others, which includes the Oze
protocol and the BoMB benchmark. CCBench is distributed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE); this derivative is distributed under the
same license. Saros, the chunk freeing, the LDBC SNB Q2 driver and the
correctness tools were added to it; the protocols and workloads not used by
the paper were removed.

The single-writer insert-only rule (commit cf0f2b7) and the obsolete-row
version of BoMB (commit e7ac810) come from branch fix-vldb-paper of
https://github.com/jnmt/ccbench.

The pseudo-random generator in common/random.hh is based on xoroshiro128+
by David Blackman and Sebastiano Vigna.

The following components are used as git submodules and are distributed
under their own licenses:
